1
00:00:22,898 --> 00:00:24,442
<i>Previously on Tank Chair...</i>

2
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,527
<i>While protecting his sister,</i>

3
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:32,199
<i>the city's strongest assassin,
Nagi, was rendered comatose.</i>

4
00:00:33,451 --> 00:00:36,162
<i>Only one thing can awaken him.</i>

5
00:00:37,496 --> 00:00:38,956
<i>And that is "killing intent."</i>

6
00:00:43,085 --> 00:00:43,919
KILL

7
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:45,421
KILL KILL KILL

8
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,759
That's some good medicine.

9
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:53,596
I haven't felt this awake in ages.

10
00:00:58,601 --> 00:01:02,271
<i>Cornered by the Academy,
Nagi and Shizuka resolve to fight Sensei,</i>

11
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:08,486
<i>the one
with the strongest killing intent of all.</i>

12
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:13,157
<i>Their only chance of beating him</i>

13
00:01:13,949 --> 00:01:16,911
<i>was to turn to Dr. Radio,
the designer of the Tank Chair,</i>

14
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:22,583
<i>to complete the legendary No Mark...</i>

15
00:01:23,042 --> 00:01:24,585
<i>Don't do anything stupid.</i>

16
00:01:24,877 --> 00:01:27,087
<i>Hole up somewhere quick.</i>

17
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:30,132
<i>Huh?!</i>

18
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:32,676
Coming through!

19
00:01:40,351 --> 00:01:44,063
Hey, what's with these guys?
You sure we're on the right route?

20
00:01:44,605 --> 00:01:47,191
They weren't here before.

21
00:01:55,074 --> 00:01:57,910
W... We're here.

22
00:01:59,245 --> 00:02:00,704
What a pair of idiots.

23
00:03:34,298 --> 00:03:38,218
{\an8}15 YEARS AGO - NEAR THE BORDER
OF A CERTAIN COUNTRY

24
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:48,187
Take that!

25
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,190
Woohoo!

26
00:04:11,377 --> 00:04:12,294
Agh!

27
00:04:23,931 --> 00:04:25,182
Hm?

28
00:04:26,809 --> 00:04:28,394
What is it, Captain?

29
00:04:30,396 --> 00:04:31,689
You go on ahead.

30
00:04:37,403 --> 00:04:39,029
<i>I can't...</i>

31
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:52,710
So there's still
one of you filthy rats left after all.

32
00:04:58,048 --> 00:05:00,259
<i>Wh... Who is it?</i>

33
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:04,888
And this takes care of all of you.

34
00:05:21,405 --> 00:05:22,906
<i>Big bro!</i>

35
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:28,662
Ahhh, that feels better.

36
00:05:31,749 --> 00:05:35,044
{\an8}THREE YEARS AGO - GUICHENG ISLAND

37
00:05:50,059 --> 00:05:51,810
Are you Dr. Radio?

38
00:05:55,773 --> 00:05:57,566
"Dr. Radio."

39
00:05:57,816 --> 00:06:02,404
You got your nickname 'cos you remotely
control animals using brainwaves, right?

40
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:11,371
Hey, is that what
those head antenna things are for?

41
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,874
So where's your real body?
Here on Guicheng?

42
00:06:14,041 --> 00:06:17,627
What's a genius who became
a science ministry chief in their teens

43
00:06:17,628 --> 00:06:19,379
doing in a place like this?

44
00:06:19,713 --> 00:06:21,506
Hey, you hungry?

45
00:06:21,507 --> 00:06:22,800
Want some dog food?

46
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:28,097
Hey...

47
00:06:32,643 --> 00:06:37,731
Oh, hello, is that "Rack 'Em & Stack 'Em
Animal Control 911"?

48
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:42,902
I'd like you to do something about
a filthy stray dog that spies on people...

49
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:44,696
- It's at--
- <i>Hey!</i>

50
00:06:45,656 --> 00:06:49,159
See? I thought so!

51
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,954
<i>What's with you? What do you want?</i>

52
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:55,916
I want you to make me something.

53
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:04,424
If you help me out,

54
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:07,970
I'll kill that guy for you.

55
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:11,223
That guy just now...

56
00:07:11,598 --> 00:07:15,018
He's the boss of that mercenary group
famous across Guicheng, right?

57
00:07:15,727 --> 00:07:18,480
I don't know what kinda grudge
you've got against him.

58
00:07:18,689 --> 00:07:21,691
But he's protected 24/7,

59
00:07:21,692 --> 00:07:27,823
so going up against him when you're not
a pro assassin is kinda nuts.

60
00:07:32,536 --> 00:07:37,374
<i>So what's this thing
you want me to make you?</i>

61
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:42,504
Your specialty is, uh...

62
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:48,301
"supplementing bodily functions
through applied mechanical engineering,

63
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:51,805
and researching specialized care
and assistance"... right?

64
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:55,934
<i>So what if it is?</i>

65
00:07:56,852 --> 00:07:59,771
I think you can help me, then.

66
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:03,442
A wheelchair.

67
00:08:04,693 --> 00:08:09,948
I want one you can use for killing.

68
00:08:30,636 --> 00:08:32,304
What's with her?

69
00:08:36,141 --> 00:08:39,937
<i>In the end, I designed
seven specialized wheelchairs</i>

70
00:08:40,062 --> 00:08:43,232
<i>for this strange girl, Shizuka,
and her brother Nagi</i>

71
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:48,779
<i>so that they could adapt
to any situation in a fight.</i>

72
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:55,994
<i>And to conceal his identity,
given his extremely unusual condition,</i>

73
00:08:56,912 --> 00:09:00,165
<i>I also suggested
he wear a mask during "rehab."</i>

74
00:09:01,667 --> 00:09:06,213
<i>And then, the night my work was complete,</i>

75
00:09:06,922 --> 00:09:09,675
<i>my revenge came to an abrupt end.</i>

76
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:16,181
<i>A monster who sought ever stronger foes
to devour their "killing intent" was born.</i>

77
00:09:17,266 --> 00:09:19,268
<i>A monster called "Tank Chair."</i>

78
00:09:22,354 --> 00:09:26,191
For crying out loud... I said no!

79
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:28,819
You're going up against a group

80
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:34,157
that governments everywhere
keep under the strictest surveillance.

81
00:09:34,825 --> 00:09:40,205
Unless you want to die, go underground
and get plastic surgery right now.

82
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:43,542
I know, I know,
it's our old school, after all.

83
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:48,171
See, Nagi's saying "Please help us," too.

84
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:51,174
Ugh, don't play with your brother
when he's comatose!

85
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:57,264
You're such a softie, Doc.

86
00:09:57,848 --> 00:09:58,724
Huh?

87
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:04,187
You're hesitating
because you don't want us to die, right?

88
00:10:06,648 --> 00:10:07,983
I noticed, you know.

89
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:13,113
You kept watching over us
even after the Tank Chairs were complete.

90
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:16,742
<i>It was unlike me,
but I couldn't just walk away.</i>

91
00:10:19,911 --> 00:10:25,292
<i>Like me, she'd lost her big brother
because of her own actions.</i>

92
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:27,669
Thank you.

93
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,171
But...

94
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:33,759
We made this decision together.
We'll stand and fight.

95
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:40,932
So trying to sway you
is a waste of time, then.

96
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:42,559
So...

97
00:10:42,726 --> 00:10:43,727
I mean...

98
00:10:44,353 --> 00:10:48,440
I should be able to get some good data,
so I'll help you out a bit.

99
00:10:49,358 --> 00:10:52,235
But the situation's less than ideal.

100
00:10:53,028 --> 00:10:57,866
Their network covers
almost the whole of Guicheng now.

101
00:10:58,575 --> 00:11:02,536
And that mismatched boy-girl duo
leading Class C is no joke either.

102
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:06,916
Oh, the Kurosaka siblings.
So they're still on the island.

103
00:11:06,917 --> 00:11:10,629
But more importantly, the new guy
that's been added from Class A...

104
00:11:11,505 --> 00:11:15,675
He's been going around massacring
those who could be "medicine" for Nagi.

105
00:11:16,802 --> 00:11:18,970
He's taking away
Nagi's chance of recovering

106
00:11:19,304 --> 00:11:22,140
and taking control
of this dog-eat-dog island.

107
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:25,352
It's insane, but it's effective.

108
00:11:26,228 --> 00:11:30,148
And what's more, he's strong enough

109
00:11:31,108 --> 00:11:33,068
to pull it off.

110
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:38,907
Ah, he'd be the guy who spread all that
killing intent through town the other day.

111
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:43,745
So then we really need to complete
you-know-what.

112
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:46,248
The No Mark, huh?

113
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:49,709
<i>A wheelchair that doesn't just supplement,</i>

114
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:53,296
<i>but goes beyond the body's limits.</i>

115
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:56,425
<i>It has the potential for mass destruction,</i>

116
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,969
<i>but the strain on the operator
is immeasurable.</i>

117
00:11:59,261 --> 00:12:00,595
<i>That's why it was shelved.</i>

118
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:06,351
It's true, the No Mark's your only choice
if you're going up against the Academy.

119
00:12:08,270 --> 00:12:09,479
But...

120
00:12:10,105 --> 00:12:14,109
I know. There's stuff you need, right?

121
00:12:15,152 --> 00:12:16,319
<i>Meta Metal.</i>

122
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:20,614
<i>A mineral-based semi-living organism
that changes shape and hardness</i>

123
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:22,409
<i>in response to human brainwaves.</i>

124
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:24,828
<i>And the "ignition key."</i>

125
00:12:25,454 --> 00:12:30,876
<i>The killing intent of 100 people directed
at the operator, Nagi, for three minutes.</i>

126
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:35,671
Hey, it'll work out somehow.

127
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,757
We'll just get Nagi to tough it out.

128
00:13:02,491 --> 00:13:04,367
Move it! They're gaining on us!

129
00:13:40,946 --> 00:13:46,660
I have found bushido lies
not in immediate capture, but in torment!

130
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,162
Let us out!

131
00:13:51,164 --> 00:13:54,000
Let us out! Let us out!

132
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:59,297
Dammit!

133
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,555
There's no escape for you!

134
00:14:07,556 --> 00:14:13,311
As far as society is concerned,
you Guicheng street children don't exist.

135
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:16,523
So you can be sold for a good price
outside the island!

136
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:27,700
Don't give up!

137
00:14:27,701 --> 00:14:28,868
Keep going!

138
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,253
You go ahead.

139
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:41,840
Get... real...

140
00:15:13,788 --> 00:15:18,168
MARK II: "THE SWORD"

141
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:23,089
Tank Chair Mark II.

142
00:15:24,299 --> 00:15:25,382
"The Sword."

143
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:26,968
TANK CHAIR MARK II: "THE SWORD"

144
00:15:35,769 --> 00:15:36,770
What was that?

145
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:40,482
Wh... Who knows?

146
00:15:40,774 --> 00:15:41,774
Who's that?!

147
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:43,985
He's carrying a sword!

148
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:46,904
An interloper!

149
00:15:46,905 --> 00:15:49,366
He means to interfere?

150
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:52,160
Then kill him!

151
00:15:53,036 --> 00:15:54,204
KILL KILL KILL

152
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:47,173
Im... possible...

153
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:53,388
In... deed...

154
00:16:58,101 --> 00:16:59,269
Wow!

155
00:17:01,563 --> 00:17:02,981
Who is that guy?!

156
00:17:05,984 --> 00:17:08,402
My lord! My lord!

157
00:17:08,403 --> 00:17:09,988
Wake up!

158
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:19,539
Doc, did any of those guys
have any meta metal on them?

159
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:21,624
<i>No, none of them.</i>

160
00:17:24,002 --> 00:17:29,507
You fool... I am Yoshitsune,
head of Neo-Bushido!

161
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:33,845
You dare commit this outrage against me?!

162
00:17:35,764 --> 00:17:41,936
You shall be rust
upon my cursed blade, Muramasa-X!

163
00:17:44,856 --> 00:17:49,944
Muramasa, heed my will!

164
00:17:58,661 --> 00:18:00,205
The sword's shape...!

165
00:18:00,497 --> 00:18:05,335
Muramasa, Mode: Axe.

166
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:17,597
Hngh!

167
00:18:17,847 --> 00:18:20,475
Little pest, scurrying around like that...

168
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:24,062
Mode: Spear.

169
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:29,025
Crap!

170
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:51,548
Th... That's insane!

171
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:56,803
Catching my blade with one hand?

172
00:18:57,345 --> 00:18:58,888
Return!

173
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:03,476
<i>A metal-based semi-living organism
that changes shape with brainwaves.</i>

174
00:19:04,018 --> 00:19:07,021
<i>There's no doubt about it,
that sword's Meta Metal.</i>

175
00:19:07,230 --> 00:19:09,816
Hm... I see...

176
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:15,864
Well then, I'll take it from him.

177
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:22,120
He threw away his scabbard!

178
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:27,458
Coming straight toward me like that.
How dare you!

179
00:19:28,293 --> 00:19:31,129
Muramasa Ougi...

180
00:19:31,546 --> 00:19:33,923
Mt. Tsurugi.

181
00:19:35,466 --> 00:19:37,677
I have found that bushido

182
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:42,348
is the art of killing!

183
00:19:46,269 --> 00:19:48,271
<i>From the ground?! What do we do?</i>

184
00:19:48,479 --> 00:19:50,063
- Sorry, Doc.
- <i>Huh?</i>

185
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:51,482
I'm gonna need some repairs.

186
00:19:58,448 --> 00:19:59,866
A <i>kamaitachi</i> strike?!

187
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:09,792
Only a plasma cutter can cut through
this layered titanium shell!

188
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:21,220
<i>The gap in my armor...</i>

189
00:20:22,472 --> 00:20:24,724
<i>That's what he was aiming for all along.</i>

190
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:28,311
Bravo!

191
00:20:29,187 --> 00:20:30,146
Magnificent.

192
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:47,246
<i>That takes care of the Meta Metal, then.</i>

193
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:49,499
<i>Now...</i>

194
00:20:55,004 --> 00:20:57,382
W... We're saved?

195
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:05,723
I'd say there are about 70 or 80 of you.

196
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,312
Who is that guy?

197
00:21:13,189 --> 00:21:14,816
Tank Chair.

198
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:19,861
He helps the weak...
well he kinda does, maybe.

199
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:22,489
But he crushes the strong for sure.

200
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:24,867
The hero of Guicheng.

201
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:27,286
Tank Chair...?

202
00:21:28,121 --> 00:21:29,872
Wh... Who are you?

203
00:21:30,248 --> 00:21:34,002
Huh? I'm, like...

204
00:21:34,877 --> 00:21:38,089
his manager... kind of?

205
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:42,385
By the way, do you guys...

206
00:21:43,428 --> 00:21:46,848
wanna join the Tank Chair fan club?

207
00:21:57,442 --> 00:22:01,988
Those siblings... I never thought
they'd actually pull it off...

208
00:22:05,158 --> 00:22:10,621
Now then, let's get back to it, shall we?

209
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,936
{\an8}ILLUSTRATION BY: TAIKI KAWAKAMI

210
00:23:57,937 --> 00:24:00,940
{\an8}SUBTITLES BY: MARDI MIYAKE

